          <mxGeometry height="48" width="48" x="120" y="894" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r5-awsCre-text" parent="1" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontColor=#827717;spacingLeft=10;" value="Provider Observe finds the new MR with no existing AWS record → calls &lt;b&gt;ChangeResourceRecordSets&lt;/b&gt; with action=&lt;b&gt;CREATE&lt;/b&gt; on the same hosted zone&#xa;New record set is added with the new type / routing policy / values — &lt;b&gt;DNS gap ends here&lt;/b&gt; ( typically a few seconds, plus existing-resolver-cache TTL )" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="48" width="1276" x="184" y="894" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r5-s10" parent="1" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#43A047;strokeColor=#1B5E20;fontColor=#ffffff;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;" value="10" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="32" width="32" x="20" y="986" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r5-final" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFDE7;strokeColor=#F9A825;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#827717;align=center;" value="&lt;b&gt;Final state&lt;/b&gt; — new record set live in Route 53 with the new type / routing policy. Brief DNS gap occurred between the DELETE in step 6 and the CREATE in step 9. To avoid the gap for routing-policy edits, prefer creating a new record under a different setIdentifier and retiring the old one separately." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="50" width="1380" x="80" y="980" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r5-warning" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E8EAF6;strokeColor=#3F51B5;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=8;fontStyle=2;" value="&lt;b&gt;Note&lt;/b&gt; — the destructive recreate is a deliberate safety choice in record-edit.yaml ( line 250 ). Route 53 cannot mutate type or setIdentifier on a live record set, and changing routing-policy fields can leave the resource in an inconsistent shape ; rebuilding from scratch keeps the Composition deterministic at the cost of a short DNS gap." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="1380" x="60" y="1054" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
